    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "to learn about how widespread this is. And you know this from your work in Southwestern Minnesota with the Southwest Crisis Center. This is a terrible crime that is happening right in front of our eyes, and we might not even see it. And it is with that in mind that Senator Murkowski and I teamed up on this bipartisan bill. And the purpose of the bill is to provide grants to local schools and educational organizations and community-based organizations that are working on domestic violence and sexual violence and human trafficking to help to educate people, to understand what's happening here. And it would help organizations train even children, young people, but also educators to recognize the signs of human trafficking and to put us on a path towards preventing it. And I'm excited that we've gotten some good support and it's a bipartisan bill which is of course so important when we want to move things through Congress.",
