    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75060.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "It is a lot of people. And I pay really great tribute to the Southwest Crisis Center and other places like it around the state that are working to address this issue. And it's not going away at anything. I think it's becoming more significant. The United Nations Children's Fund, UNICEF, tells us that every two minutes a child is being victimized for sexual exploitation. And this is a reminder of what a significant issue of this is that we must address. Again, the talent that I hear about is that people don't always recognize the signs of human trafficking. And the awareness of this talent has risen greatly in the last several years, but we still have work to do.",
